\section{Checking values}{


poputils has three families of functions for checking numeric
values: \verb{count_*()} for counts, \verb{prob_*()} for probabilities,
and \verb{rate_*()} for rates. Each family has a \code{diagnose} function,
which reports on each condition, and an \code{assert} function, which
raises an error if any condition is not met.
Some conditions are always checked, and others are
switched on through arguments.
All functions accept ordinary numeric vectors and \link[rvec:rvec]{rvecs}.

Apart from \code{no_na}, conditions ignore \code{NA}s.\tabular{ll}{
